From: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 23:33:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: restore beacons only after an offchannel stop

The driver uploads the beacons again after each channel set on the
operating channel. A CSA reaches that point when mac80211 moves the
link to the reserved channel context, before mac80211 ends the CSA
and installs the beacon for the new channel. The upload then carries
the CSA countdown, and the firmware starts a second countdown on the
new channel, which can end the next channel switch too early.

Upload the beacons on the operating channel only when an offchannel
dwell stopped them. The stop itself is upstream in aa2f13c3be79
("wifi: mt76: mt7996: disable beacons when going offchannel").

Signed-off-by: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt76.h        |    1 +
 mt7996/main.c |   11 +++++++++--
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/mt76.h
+++ b/mt76.h
@@ -950,6 +950,7 @@ struct mt76_phy {
 	struct cfg80211_chan_def chandef;
 	struct cfg80211_chan_def main_chandef;
 	bool offchannel;
+	bool offchan_bcn_stopped;
 	bool radar_enabled;
 	bool no_active_monitor;
 	unsigned long tx_block;
--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -734,8 +734,10 @@ int mt7996_set_channel(struct mt76_phy *
 	struct mt7996_phy *phy = mphy->priv;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (mphy->offchannel)
+	if (mphy->offchannel) {
 		mt7996_mac_update_beacons(phy);
+		mphy->offchan_bcn_stopped = true;
+	}
 
 	if (phy->dev->eeprom_mode == EEPROM_MODE_FLASH) {
 		ret = mt7996_mcu_apply_tx_dpd(phy);
@@ -767,8 +769,13 @@ int mt7996_set_channel(struct mt76_phy *
 	if (!mphy->offchannel)
 		mt7996_apply_edcca_limits(phy);
 	phy->noise = 0;
-	if (!mphy->offchannel)
+	/* a channel switch of a CSA also lands here, and a beacon upload at
+	 * that point would start a second CSA countdown on the new channel
+	 */
+	if (!mphy->offchannel && mphy->offchan_bcn_stopped) {
 		mt7996_mac_update_beacons(phy);
+		mphy->offchan_bcn_stopped = false;
+	}
 
 out:
 	ieee80211_queue_delayed_work(mphy->hw, &mphy->mac_work,
